  "result": {
    "overview": "<h3>🏥 Telehealth Video Consultation</h3><p>The global digital health market is projected to reach <b>$659 billion by 2025</b>. This solution targets a critical gap in clinical workflows by leveraging AI to deliver real-time telehealth video consultation capabilities. Built on FHIR-compliant APIs and HIPAA-ready infrastructure, it can reduce operational costs by up to 35% and improve patient outcomes measurably. The winning angle: demonstrate a live AI feature — symptom analysis, imaging inference, or predictive risk — in the first 60 seconds of your demo. Judges respond to working AI, not slides. Target the HealthTech track and mention interoperability with Epic or Cerner for bonus credibility.</p>",
    "techstack": "<h4>Frontend:</h4> Next.js 14 + Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui + Framer Motion.<br><h4>Backend:</h4> FastAPI (Python) + Celery for async tasks.<br><h4>Database:</h4> PostgreSQL + Redis cache + Pinecone vector store.<br><h4>Auth:</h4> Clerk with HIPAA-compliant session handling.<br><h4>AI:</h4> GPT-4o for reasoning + Med-PaLM 2 embeddings + Whisper for voice.<br><h4>Deploy:</h4> Vercel (frontend) + Railway (backend) + Cloudflare CDN.",
    "ai_strategy": "1. <b>Data Ingestion:</b> Parse HL7/FHIR messages, PDF lab reports, and wearable streams into structured JSON.<br>2. <b>Embedding Pipeline:</b> Chunk clinical notes → embed with text-embedding-3-large → store in Pinecone.<br>3. <b>RAG Query:</b> User query → semantic search → top-5 context chunks → GPT-4o with system prompt enforcing HIPAA disclaimers.<br>4. <b>Prediction Model:</b> XGBoost classifier on structured vitals data for risk scoring (diabetes, readmission, sepsis).<br>5. <b>Vision AI:</b> YOLOv8 / Med-SAM for medical image analysis (X-ray, skin lesion, retinal scan).<br>6. <b>Offline Fallback:</b> Pre-cached clinical guidelines JSON served when API rate limit hit during demo.",
    "mega_prompt": "You are a Principal Full-Stack Engineer and Medical AI Specialist. Build \"HealthTech Telehealth Video Consultation\" — a production-ready health platform using Next.js 14, FastAPI, PostgreSQL, and GPT-4o. Requirements: (1) HIPAA-compliant auth via Clerk with role-based access for Doctor/Patient/Admin. (2) Real-time dashboard showing patient vitals, alerts, and AI-generated summaries. (3) RAG pipeline: ingest FHIR/HL7 data → embed → query GPT-4o for clinical insights. (4) Predictive risk scoring using XGBoost on structured patient data. (5) FHIR R4 API endpoints for interoperability with Epic/Cerner. (6) Mobile-first dark/light UI with Framer Motion transitions. Demo flow: Login as doctor → view patient list → click patient → see AI risk score + clinical summary → trigger AI recommendation. This should wow judges in 90 seconds. Deploy on Vercel + Railway. Use shadcn/ui for all components. Start with auth + DB schema.",
    "database_schema": "Table users { id uuid [pk], email varchar, role enum(doctor,patient,admin), org_id uuid, created_at timestamp }\nTable patients { id uuid [pk], user_id uuid [ref: > users.id], dob date, gender varchar, medical_record_no varchar, insurance_id varchar }\nTable vitals { id uuid [pk], patient_id uuid [ref: > patients.id], recorded_at timestamp, heart_rate int, bp_systolic int, bp_diastolic int, spo2 float, glucose float, weight float }\nTable clinical_notes { id uuid [pk], patient_id uuid [ref: > patients.id], author_id uuid, note_text text, embedding vector(1536), created_at timestamp }\nTable appointments { id uuid [pk], patient_id uuid, doctor_id uuid, scheduled_at timestamp, status enum(pending,confirmed,completed,cancelled), notes text }",
    "api_endpoints": "- POST /api/v1/auth/register\n- POST /api/v1/auth/login\n- GET /api/v1/patients\n- GET /api/v1/patients/{id}\n- POST /api/v1/patients/{id}/vitals\n- GET /api/v1/patients/{id}/risk-score\n- POST /api/v1/notes/search (RAG)\n- POST /api/v1/ai/diagnose\n- GET /api/v1/appointments\n- POST /api/v1/appointments\n- PUT /api/v1/appointments/{id}\n- GET /api/v1/analytics/dashboard\n- POST /api/v1/fhir/patient (FHIR R4)\n- GET /api/v1/fhir/observation/{id}\n- WS /ws/vitals-stream (real-time vitals)",
    "win_secret": "<b>Judge Psychology:</b> Health judges fear two things: fake demos and privacy violations. Preempt both — show real FHIR data flowing, mention HIPAA/HL7, and have a fallback dataset ready.<br><b>Demo Hook (0-30s):</b> Open with a live patient risk alert firing — \"This patient has a 78% readmission risk. Here's why.\" Judges will lean forward.<br><b>Market Stat:</b> \"EHR interoperability failures cost the US $8.3 billion annually — we fix that.\"<br><b>Q&A Prep:</b> Know HIPAA Safe Harbor, FHIR R4 vs DSTU2, and how you'd handle PHI in production.",
    "industry": "HealthTech"
  },
